hadiths[42]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15694","Abu Said, the freed slave of Banu Hashim, and Hasan said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Zabban, Hasan said in his hadith: Zabban ibn Faid narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever steps over the Muslims on Friday is taken as a bridge to Hell."
"15695","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, Zabban ibn Faid al-Hubrani narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Muadh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father Muadh ibn Anas al-Juhani, the Companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever reads Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad until he completes it ten times, Allah builds for him a palace in Paradise. So Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Then I will increase, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah is more and better."
"15696","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to me, from Zabban, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever reads a thousand verses in the path of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will be written on the Day of Resurrection with the prophets and the truthful and the martyrs and the righteous, and excellent those as companions, if Allah Almighty wills."
"15697","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, and Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, from Zabban, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever guards behind the Muslims in the path of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, voluntarily, no ruler seizes him, will not see the Fire with his eyes except to fulfill the oath, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: And there is none of you except will come to it."
"15698","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: Rishdin narrated to us, from Zabban, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Indeed remembrance in the path of Allah Almighty is multiplied above spending by seven hundred fold. Yahya said in his hadith: by seven hundred thousand fold."
"15699","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that a man asked him and said: Which jihad is greatest in reward. He said: Most of them in remembrance of Allah, Blessed and Exalted. He said: Which fasting people are greatest in reward. He said: Most of them in remembrance of Allah, Blessed and Exalted. Then he mentioned to us prayer and alms tax and pilgrimage and charity, all that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, says: Most of them in remembrance of Allah, Blessed and Exalted. So Abu Bakr said to Umar: O Abu Hafs, those who remember have gone with all good. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Yes."
"15700","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Muadh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: It is due upon one who stands over a gathering to greet them, and it is due upon one who rises from a gathering to greet. A man stood while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was speaking, and did not greet. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: How quickly he forgot."
"15701","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever builds a building without injustice or transgression, or plants a plant without injustice or transgression, he will have a continuing reward as long as any of Allah's creation, blessed and exalted is He, benefits from it."
"15702","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Zabban, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever gives for Allah the Exalted, and withholds for Allah the Exalted, and loves for Allah the Exalted, and hates for Allah the Exalted, and marries for Allah the Exalted, has completed his faith."
"15703","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The best of virtues are that you join ties with the one who cut you off, and give to the one who withheld from you, and pardon the one who insulted you."
"15704","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever suppresses his anger while he is able to take revenge, Allah, blessed and exalted is He, will call him before all creatures until He gives him the choice among the houris whichever he wishes. And whoever refrains from wearing fine clothes while he is able to do so, out of humility for Allah, blessed and exalted is He, Allah, blessed and exalted is He, will call him before all creatures until Allah the Exalted gives him the choice among the garments of faith whichever he wishes."
"15705","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: When you hear the caller announcing the prayer, say as he says."
"15706","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Zabban, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: The one who laughs in prayer, and the one who turns, and the one who cracks his fingers, are in one same standing."
"15707","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, Sahl narrated to us, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he ordered his companions to go out for battle, and that a man stayed behind and said to his family: I will stay behind until I pray Zuhr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I will greet him and bid him farewell, so he will supplicate for me with a supplication that will intercede on the Day of Resurrection. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, the man came forward greeting him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you know by how much your companions have preceded you? He said: Yes, they preceded me by their morning departure. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, they have preceded you by farther than what is between the two easts and the two wests in virtue."
"15708","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever sits in his place of prayer after praying Fajr until he glorifies in Duha, saying nothing but good, his sins will be forgiven even if they are more than the foam of the sea."
"15709","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated to us, from Sahl, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Shall I not inform you why Allah, blessed and exalted is He, named Ibrahim His close friend, the one who fulfilled? Because he used to say every morning and evening: So glory be to Allah when you enter the evening and when you enter the morning, until he completes the verse."
"15710","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say when he departed: All praise is due to Allah Who has not taken a son and has had no partner in dominion, to the end of the surah."
"15711","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever recites the beginning of Surah al-Kahf and its end, it will be a light for him from his feet to his head, and whoever recites it all, it will be a light for him between the heaven and the earth."
"15712","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, Sahl narrated to us, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: All estrangement, and disbelief, and hypocrisy is for one who hears Allah's caller calling to prayer, inviting to success, and does not answer him."
"15713","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The Ummah will remain upon the Shariah as long as three things do not appear among them: as long as knowledge is not taken away from them, and the children of sin do not increase among them, and the Saqqarun do not appear among them. He said: And what are the Saqqarun, or the Saqlawun, O Messenger of Allah? He said: People who will be at the end of time, whose greeting among them is mutual cursing."
"15714","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he passed by people standing upon their beasts and mounts, and said to them: Ride them safe and leave them safe, and do not take them as chairs for your conversations in the roads and markets, for many a ridden beast is better than its rider and remembers Allah, blessed and exalted is He, more than him."
"15715","Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun informed me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade sitting hugging the knees on Friday while the Imam is delivering the sermon."
"15716","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons clothing while he is able to afford it, out of humility for Allah, blessed and exalted is He, Allah, blessed and exalted is He, will call him on the Day of Resurrection before all creatures until He gives him the choice among the garments of faith whichever he wishes."
"15717","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Marhum narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats food then says: All praise is due to Allah Who fed me this and provided me with it without any power or strength from me, Allah will forgive him his past sins."
"15718","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, from Zabban, from Sahl, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a woman came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, my husband went out raiding, and I used to follow his prayer when he prayed and all his deeds, so inform me of a deed that will make me reach his deed until he returns. He said to her: Can you stand without sitting, and fast without breaking, and remember Allah, blessed and exalted is He, without flagging, until he returns? She said: I cannot do this, O Messenger of Allah. He said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, if you were able to do it, you would not reach a tenth of his deed until he returns."
"15719","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, from Zabban, from Sahl, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The verse of might is: All praise is due to Allah Who has not taken a son, the whole verse."
"15720","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, from Zabban, from Sahl, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand people are safe."
"15721","Yahya narrated to us, he said: Rishdin narrated to us, from Zabban, from Sahl, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Indeed Allah, blessed and exalted is He, has servants whom Allah will not speak to on the Day of Resurrection, nor purify them, nor look at them. It was said to him: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: One who disowns his parents turning away from them, and one who disowns his child, and a man whom people favored then he denied their favor and disowned them."
"15722","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Marhum narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever suppresses anger while he is able to carry it out, Allah, blessed and exalted is He, will call him before all creatures until He gives him the choice from whichever of the houris he wishes."
"15723","Abd Allah ibn Yazid narrated to us from his memory, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub Abu Yahya narrated to me, he said: Abu Marhum Abd al-Rahim ibn Maymun narrated to me, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh al-Juhani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives for Allah the Exalted, and withholds for Allah, and loves for Allah, and hates for Allah, and marries for Allah, has completed his faith."
"15724","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, and he was among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ride these beasts safe and leave them safe, and do not take them as chairs."
"15725","Hajjaj narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, he said: Zabban ibn Fa'id narrated to me, from Ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of that."
"15726","He said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, and he had companionship, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ride these beasts safe and leave them safe, and do not take them as chairs."
"15727","Hasan narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever was fasting and visited a sick person and witnessed a funeral, he will be forgiven, unless he commits anew afterwards."
"15728","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: That I escort a warrior in the path of Allah and provide him with a mount morning or evening is more beloved to me than the world and what is in it."
"15729","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Indeed the safe one is the one from whose hand and tongue people are safe."
"15730","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah the Mighty, a seedling will be planted for him in Paradise. And whoever recites the Quran and completes it and acts upon what is in it, his parents will be clothed on the Day of Resurrection with a crown that is better than the light of the sun in the houses of this world, had it been among them. So what do you think of the one who acted upon it?"
"15731","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Zabban narrated to us, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he passed by people standing upon their beasts and mounts, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Ride them safe and leave them safe, and do not take them as chairs for your conversations in the roads and markets, for many a ridden beast is better than its rider, it remembers Allah the Exalted more than him."
"15732","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Khayr ibn Nu'aym al-Hadrami, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remembrance excels spending in the path of Allah, blessed and exalted is He, by seven hundred thousand fold."
"15733","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Khath'ami, from Farwah ibn Mujahid al-Lakhmi, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh al-Juhani, from his father, he said: We camped at Hisn Sinan in the land of Rome with Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Malik, and the people constricted the dwellings and cut off the road. Mu'adh said: O people, we raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such and such battle, and the people constricted the road, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a caller who called out: Whoever constricts a dwelling or cuts off a road, there is no jihad for him."
"15734","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj and Ya'mur ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ahmad said: Abd Allah informed us, and Ya'mur said: Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Sulayman, that Ismail ibn Yahya al-Ma'afiri informed him, from Sahl ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas al-Juhani, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever protects a believer from a hypocrite disparaging him, Allah, blessed and exalted is He, will send an angel protecting his flesh on the Day of Resurrection from the Fire of Hell. And whoever accuses a believer of something seeking to shame him, Allah the Exalted will detain him on the bridge of Hell until he exits from what he said."
"15735","Hasan narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from Ibn Mu'adh ibn Anas, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take beasts as chairs, for many a ridden beast is more remembering of Allah the Exalted than its rider."
